 ## Error patterns (false-SAFE signatures)
 
-- **Unpushed-lane trap**: `git worktree list` says `prunable`, but
-  `git log --branches --not --remotes --oneline` in the owning repo is
-  non-empty → the worktree metadata is NOT safe to prune yet; classify the
-  *commits* first. Live instance: kotodama-shokunin 2026-10-18 (round-17..22
-  unpushed, dirty tree, 553M `.scratch/`).
-- **Superseded-snapshot drift**: a config copy claimed "byte-identical" that
-  `cmp` shows differing from the live file — it is a stale *snapshot*, not a
-  duplicate; classify as `stale` only after diff shows it holds no unique
-  edits. Live instance: `shokunin.conf.full-roster-20261015` vs live
-  `shokunin.conf` (3859 vs 4092 B, 2026-10-18).
-- **Checkpoint-blob bloat**: fleet-root commits like `b2f2efa` that land
-  launch JSON / PNG checkpoint files at the fleet root — classify per file;
-  if pushed, they qualify for `pushed` receipts individually.
-- **Worktree-with-unique-commits**: `git worktree list` + `git log <wt-sha> --oneline | head` —
-  a prunable worktree whose tip has commits not on any branch is NOT-SAFE.
+- **Unpushed-lane trap.** `git worktree list` can say `prunable` while the repo-root verifier reports `unpushed` or `dirty`. That verdict is `NOT-SAFE`. Size is not a receipt; mint-time scratch sizes are retired. Re-run `tools/souji-verify.sh --json <repo>`. Do not prune.
+- **Hardcoded default branch.** Do not test a literal `origin/main` and do not fetch inside the receipt command. Resolve `refs/remotes/origin/HEAD`, or the single remote-tracking ref, or refuse.
+- **Local-master fallback.** Zero `refs/remotes/origin/*` must not become `SAFE(pushed)` from `refs/heads/master`. Both tools refuse. Trust the `NOT-SAFE` line.
+- **Named-branch before unique=0.** An absent worktree directory with unique commits = 0 against `--all` is still `NOT-SAFE(unpushed-branch)` when its named branch has commits not on any remote-tracking ref. Do not prune from unique=0 alone. Re-run the verifier on the registration path.
+- **Hidden stale reference.** `SAFE(stale)` with `refs=0` can be a false-SAFE when the only live mention is in a hidden file. The `--hidden` operator gate is mandatory before removal.
+- **Symlink digest.** A directory whose digest scope contains a symlink is `symlink-present`, not `SAFE(moved-to-obsidian)`.
+- **Deleted-path ancestry.** An introducing commit on the default ref is not a receipt if the path is already gone. `souji-verify.sh` returns `unreachable`. Re-verify existence at correction time.
+- **Superseded snapshot.** A config copy that `cmp` shows differs from the live file is not a duplicate. That note does not override the verifier. If the introducing commit is on the resolved remote default ref, the receipt is `pushed`, not `stale`.
 
